# Motor joint definition, ported from upstream b2MotorJointDef and
# b2DefaultMotorJointDef in types.h and joint.c. Defaults match upstream:
# zero offsets, one newton maximum force, one newton-metre maximum torque,
# 0.3 correction factor. The joint drives body B toward a pose relative to
# body A rather than holding anchors together.
Class MotorJointDefinition
## First attached body, ported from b2MotorJointDef.bodyIdA.
Property BodyA As Body
## Second attached body, driven toward the offset pose.
Property BodyB As Body
## Target position of body B minus body A in body A's frame, in metres.
Property LinearOffset As Vector2
## Target body B angle minus body A angle in radians.
Property AngularOffset As Double
## Maximum linear force magnitude, typically in newtons.
Property MaxForce As Double
## Maximum torque magnitude, typically in newton-metres.
Property MaxTorque As Double
## Position correction factor in [0, 1]; higher values close the pose gap
## faster. Clamped to the range like upstream.
Property CorrectionFactor As Double
## True when the two connected bodies may collide.
Property CollideConnected As Boolean
## User data owned by the application, copied to the created joint. Never
## read by the solver.
Property UserData As Object

## Creates a definition with upstream defaults.
Constructor()
Me.BodyA = Nothing
Me.BodyB = Nothing
Me.LinearOffset = New Vector2(0.0, 0.0)
Me.AngularOffset = 0.0
Me.MaxForce = 1.0
Me.MaxTorque = 1.0
Me.CorrectionFactor = 0.3
Me.CollideConnected = False
Me.UserData = Nothing
End Constructor
End Class
